THE XAUUSD THREE (rr=1.5/wb=12, rr=1.5/wb=8, rr=2.0/wb=12), 0.034194 of risk_frac since
2026-09-11. Two causes in sequence:
  (i) until 2026-09-22T00:29 the gateway log carries 380 refusals EACH of
      "certified cell 'XAUUSD.session_range_breakout.rr=1.5_wb=12' is not in the docket on this
      box" -- stage no_inputs, every pass. That one has since resolved itself: run today,
      _params_from_certificate returns ({'rr': 1.5, 'wait_bars': 12}, '') for all three. The
      bare-family defect of 2026-09-15 is NOT what is holding them; it was fixed and these rows
      carry the parameterised cell.
  (ii) and then they went silent instead of trading, which is this commit. family_signal_step
      keeps only signals whose time == last_bar, so the family must be ABLE to emit there. The
      2026-09-15 `signal_bars` fix appended the forming bar, which reaches a family whose loop
      ends at len(d) - 1. Every family in families_orthogonal.py ends at -1 and every one of
      them places (discovered, overnight_gap_decay, carry: 254 order intents). All 27 families
      in families.py end at len(h1) - 2 and need one MORE bar, and session_range_breakout is
      the only families.py family ever promoted LIVE.

      Measured on the box's own XAUUSD H1 bars, walking the last 240 hourly passes exactly as
      resolve_family_order builds them:

          passes where the family emitted something   240 / 240   (28 distinct signal bars)
          signals AT last_bar, frame as handed today      0
          signals AT last_bar, one more trailing bar     10

      The entry condition was met constantly. The filter matched nothing because the loop bound
      stops one index short of the bar the gateway is asking about. extend_signal_tail pads the
      frame to FAMILY_TAIL_SLACK trailing rows with copies of its own last row; no family reads
      them (the bound stops before them, every indicator is backward-looking rolling/ewm, and
      the one whole-frame aggregate is a per-date max/min for which duplicating a value already
      present is the identity), and a signal emitted ON a pad is discarded by the same
      time == last_bar filter. signal_bars=None still means `closed`, so shadow_forward and
      every hunt16 caller and the forward clocks that certified these cells are untouched.

THE USDJPY ROW is a different cause entirely and not this one: "LIVE POLICY refused
usdjpy_session_range_breakout_asia_rr25_wb12: USDJPY is outside the live sleeve universe
['XAUUSD']", 16:44 and 16:45 today. data/live_sleeve_policy.json was rewritten at 18:30Z to admit
USDJPY, so that door is already open -- it then hit the same off-by-one behind it.

THE DIRECTIONAL RULE, because three more XAUUSD rows land beside three gold bracket windows.
family_session_range_breakout appends a LONG at the range high and a SHORT at the range low on
one bar -- one OCO breakout, one leg taken -- and family_signal_step took sigs[-1], which is the
order the family happens to append in, so the sleeve was structurally always SHORT. E8 lost 1,135
today because three windows shorted gold together; three more rows hard-wired short is that shape
again. prefer_side places the leg that AGREES with the book's held direction and skips only the
opposing one. It chooses WHICH leg, never whether: the same one order is sent either way, and
prefer_side=None keeps sigs[-1] exactly. No cap, veto or throttle is added -- same_side_count,
leg_balance, the 0.85R break-even floor and stop_rests_at_venue already govern this lane.

E8 IS GATED ON REALISED FILLS (principal, today: "Make them all trade in mt5 account first if
they're doing well we put them on e8 too"). e8_book.mirror admits a family row only when account
495044 has recorded >= 5 realised closed trades under its name with realised R summing positive,
read from the broker's own deals. It is measured, so promotion stays automatic: the next E8-Book
pass admits a sleeve the moment it clears, with nobody acting. The gold bracket windows are
routed to gold_windows BEFORE the test, so E8's gold lane and its existing gross are untouched;
the gate can only withhold a sleeve that has never filled anywhere. The broker truncates the
sleeve to 27 characters in the order comment -- the ledger's only identity, since magic is one
desk-wide constant -- so the join is by prefix and a prefix shared by several LIVE rows is
reported as ambiguous_with rather than guessed.

AND THESE CERTIFICATES FAIL THE HONEST BAR. All 15 session_range_breakout certificates: best
Sharpe 0.1914 against sr0 0.3122, 0 of 15 above it. They are being wired up anyway on one
